  Delta^(d+1) reproduces every recorded zero; Delta^d misses 4 of 4.
  recurrence == binomial Delta^(d+1) at every (r, d>=1) cell of every rebuilt table: yes

  CONVENTION, pinned: O45's depth-0 row N(r) = pi(F[r]) - pi(F[r-1])
  is one backward difference of the cumulative ladder, for every
  base including sqrt(2).  The mode exponent is therefore n = d+1:
      z_k(b,r,d) = b^(r*rho_k) * (1 - b^(-rho_k))^(d+1) / rho_k
  (The table reads pi at floor(b^r); the mode models the count at
  the exact point b^r - under one integer per rung, no phase touched.)

