4. THE STATISTIC, AND THE CONFOUND STATED BEFORE THE NUMBERS
==============================================================================
  delta_k = Delta * gamma_k + psi_k, where Delta = r_A ln b_A -
  r_B ln b_B is the log window-TOP offset and psi_k carries only
  the (base, depth) geometry - the SAME psi_k for every pair in a
  matched family.  Three structural consequences, measured below:
    (i)   naive R is a function of Delta alone;
    (ii)  the fast-phase-corrected R is one number per family,
          identical at the target and every null pair;
    (iii) a non-overlapping pair needs |Delta| >= the shorter
          window, so a position-matched non-overlap null cannot
          exist when the observed |Delta| is smaller than that.

